{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-77543" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the coordinates of the point ${A}^{′}$, the image of $A(-1,1)$ under the action of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/state.json" "file_sha256" "29466f38154780dd93683e3031f3c00c5fe3fef3fc8fb3b59adb43e2de760daa"} {"question" "q-77543" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the image of $A$ under the action of $T$, we first create a column-vector $x$ containing the coordinates of $A:$\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $x$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $Tx:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Tx & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result, $Tx,$ contains the coordinates of ${A}^{′}.$ Therefore, ${A}^{′}(2,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/state.json" "file_sha256" "29466f38154780dd93683e3031f3c00c5fe3fef3fc8fb3b59adb43e2de760daa"} {"question" "q-77543" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1c51e49536a811c52da04573453ecaf29d405a6bb4368af15d5a0ff0c364ff3f"} {"question" "q-77543" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/state.json" "file_sha256" "29466f38154780dd93683e3031